"mjx-n\" space=\"2\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn><mjx-mo class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c5D\"></mjx-c></mjx-mo></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span> and never decreases\nwhen a term is added. Why does that last property make it a poor basis\nfor choosing a model?</p>","file":"ch34-exponential-families-glm/05-deviance-and-inference.html"}